{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c61d","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07664-b32a-7b03-be28-978067559ac9"},"sequence":361,"recorded_at":1780531400000717,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"4279c805-073c-4405-a747-7b1a47e438ac","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"4279c805-073c-4405-a747-7b1a47e438ac","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"4279c805-073c-4405-a747-7b1a47e438ac"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"34f32507-d9d4-41aa-9b2e-1316ed0553b0"},"task_id":"34f32507-d9d4-41aa-9b2e-1316ed0553b0","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"34f32507-d9d4-41aa-9b2e-1316ed0553b0","chunk":"Read text file `internal/provhost/surrogate.go`.\n1|package provhost\n2|\n3|// This file is the local lone-surrogate gate for the Section 1.6 wire\n4|// bodies this package decodes. Pinned specification Section 1.6 requires\n5|// decoders to reject lone surrogate code points before canonicalization,\n6|// and the repository already enforces that rule in\n7|// internal/canonicaljson (validateSurrogateEscapes, called from\n8|// decodeStrict). This package decodes with its own strict object reader\n9|// (decodeStrictObject in protocol.go) because it must keep member-level\n10|// fault attribution (duplicate member names, the offending member) that\n11|// the shared decoder does not report, and encoding/json silently replaces\n12|// a lone \\ud800-style escape with U+FFFD instead of failing. So the gate\n13|// lives here, scans the raw frame bytes before decoding, and refuses the\n14|// same class the shared package refuses.\n15|//\n16|// The gate is deliberately a copy, not an import: internal/canonicaljson\n17|// is byte-identical shared baseline text that two unlanded stories must\n18|// not edit at once, so neither story may add an export there. The\n19|// surrogate-vector sweep in surrogate_test.go drives both this gate\n20|// (through decodeStrictObject) and canonicaljson.Canonicalize over a\n21|// derived enumeration of the code-point space, so the copies cannot\n22|// drift silently: a divergence reddens there rather than passing\n23|// unnoticed. The sweep judges verdicts against the independent\n24|// implementation, never against a shared hand-written expectation.\n25|//\n26|// The gate decides the surrogate-escape question only. Malformed\n27|// escapes and unterminated strings are not its verdict: they fall\n28|// through to the JSON-syntax arms that already own them. Non-UTF-8\n29|// bytes never reach it: decodeStrictObject refuses them first,\n30|// because a raw WTF-8 surrogate encoding would otherwise slip past\n31|// this escape scanner and be silently replaced with U+FFFD by\n32|// encoding/json. A lone high surrogate is a high unit not immediately\n33|// followed by a \\uDC00–\\uDFFF escape; a lone low surrogate is a low\n34|// unit in any other position. Both are refused before any member is\n35|// read.\n36|\n37|// The gate's own range constants: the high and low surrogate halves\n38|// of the Section 1.6 verdict space. The\n39|// surrogate-vector sweep in surrogate_test.go derives its pair-second\n40|// dimension from these constants arithmetically (bounds plus and minus\n41|// small offsets), so the boundary neighborhood is enumerated from the\n42|// gate rather than from a hand-written literal: shifting a bound here\n43|// moves the swept neighborhood with it instead of silently uncovering\n44|// it. Verdicts still come from the independent implementation, never\n45|// from these constants, so a wrong bound reddens against the oracle.\n46|const (\n47|\thighSurrogateMin = 0xd800\n48|\thighSurrogateMax = 0xdbff\n49|\tlowSurrogateMin  = 0xdc00\n50|\tlowSurrogateMax  = 0xdfff\n51|)\n52|\n53|// hasLoneSurrogateEscape reports whether raw JSON bytes carry a lone\n54|// surrogate escape inside any string. The string walk mirrors the shared\n55|// package's walker (backslash handling included: a \\\\ escape consumes\n56|// both bytes, so the text \"\\\\ud800\" is backslash-plus-text, not an\n57|// escape), but only the surrogate verdict is returned.\n58|func hasLoneSurrogateEscape(input []byte) bool {\n59|\tfor index := 0; index < len(input); index++ {\n60|\t\tif input[index] != '\"' {\n61|\t\t\tcontinue\n62|\t\t}\n63|\t\tfor index++; index < len(input); index++ {\n64|\t\t\tif input[index] == '\"' {\n65|\t\t\t\tgoto stringComplete\n66|\t\t\t}\n67|\t\t\tif input[index] != '\\\\' {\n68|\t\t\t\tcontinue\n69|\t\t\t}\n70|\t\t\tindex++\n71|\t\t\tif index >= len(input) || input[index] != 'u' {\n72|\t\t\t\tcontinue\n73|\t\t\t}\n74|\t\t\tunit, end, ok := readHexUnit(input, index-1)\n75|\t\t\tif !ok {\n76|\t\t\t\t// Not a well-formed \\uXXXX escape: the\n77|\t\t\t\t// JSON-syntax arms own it, not this gate.\n78|\t\t\t\tcontinue\n79|\t\t\t}\n80|\t\t\tindex = end - 1\n81|\t\t\tif unit >= highSurrogateMin && unit <= highSurrogateMax {\n82|\t\t\t\tlow, lowEnd, ok := readHexUnit(input, end)\n83|\t\t\t\tif !ok || low < lowSurrogateMin || low > lowSurrogateMax {\n84|\t\t\t\t\treturn true\n85|\t\t\t\t}\n86|\t\t\t\tindex = lowEnd - 1\n87|\t\t\t} else if unit >= lowSurrogateMin && unit <= lowSurrogateMax {\n88|\t\t\t\treturn true\n89|\t\t\t}\n90|\t\t}\n91|\t\t// The string never closed: malformed JSON the syntax arms\n92|\t\t// refuse, so the gate claims no surrogate verdict here.\n93|\t\treturn false\n94|\tstringComplete:\n95|\t}\n96|\treturn false\n97|}\n98|\n99|// readHexUnit parses one \\uXXXX escape at input[start]. It reports false\n100|// when the bytes are not a well-formed escape; hex digits parse in\n101|// either case, matching the shared package's ParseUint base-16 read.\n102|func readHexUnit(input []byte, start int) (uint16, int, bool) {\n103|\tif start < 0 || start+6 > len(input) || input[start] != '\\\\' || input[start+1] != 'u' {\n104|\t\treturn 0, start, false\n105|\t}\n106|\tvar value uint16\n107|\tfor _, b := range input[start+2 : start+6] {\n108|\t\tvar digit byte\n109|\t\tif b >= '0' && b <= '9' {\n110|\t\t\tdigit = b - '0'\n111|\t\t} else if b >= 'a' && b <= 'f' {\n112|\t\t\tdigit = b - 'a' + 10\n113|\t\t} else if b >= 'A' && b <= 'F' {\n114|\t\t\tdigit = b - 'A' + 10\n115|\t\t} else {\n116|\t\t\treturn 0, start, false\n117|\t\t}\n118|\t\tvalue = value*16 + uint16(digit)\n119|\t}\n120|\treturn value, start + 6, true\n121|}"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c61f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07664-b32a-7b03-be28-978067559ac9"},"sequence":362,"recorded_at":1780531400000719,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"4279c805-073c-4405-a747-7b1a47e438ac","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"4279c805-073c-4405-a747-7b1a47e438ac","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"4279c805-073c-4405-a747-7b1a47e438ac"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"34f32507-d9d4-41aa-9b2e-1316ed0553b0"},"task_id":"34f32507-d9d4-41aa-9b2e-1316ed0553b0","event":{"kind":"completed","task_id":"34f32507-d9d4-41aa-9b2e-1316ed0553b0"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c621","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07664-b32a-7b03-be28-978067559ac9"},"sequence":363,"recorded_at":1780531400000721,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"4279c805-073c-4405-a747-7b1a47e438ac","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"4279c805-073c-4405-a747-7b1a47e438ac","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"4279c805-073c-4405-a747-7b1a47e438ac"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"08a74324-625a-40a3-a5b8-fa7e58c8c530"},"task_id":"08a74324-625a-40a3-a5b8-fa7e58c8c530","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"08a74324-625a-40a3-a5b8-fa7e58c8c530","chunk":"Read text file `internal/environ/measure_agreement_test.go`.\n1|package environ\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"fmt\"\n5|\t\"strings\"\n6|\t\"testing\"\n7|\n8|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/canonicaljson\"\n9|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/dirnode\"\n10|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/provhost\"\n11|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/scalar\"\n12|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/sessadapter\"\n13|)\n14|\n15|// This file is the cross-facade string-measure battery. Section\n16|// 1.6 bounds strings in characters, not bytes: string[1..128]\n17|// admits 128 characters of any width. Two strict decoders both\n18|// blind to lone surrogates was one drift class the cross-story\n19|// review found; byte-vs-rune bounds disagreeing on a member that\n20|// crosses both protocols was another. This battery pins the\n21|// measure at every character-bound member one facade shares with\n22|// another, with multibyte vectors that separate the measures: a\n23|// 128-`é` value is 128 characters but 256 bytes, so a\n24|// byte-measure refuses what the specification admits.\n25|//\n26|// The byte side is ledgered, not left open. Provider SpawnPlan\n27|// argv elements and totals and env-literal values bound BYTES by\n28|// Section 5.1 (outside this story), implemented in exactly two\n29|// functions — provhost checkSpawnArgv and checkSpawnEnvLiterals\n30|// — and the byte rows below drive all three byte gates through\n31|// the production DecodeSpawnPlan entry. validEnvName measures\n32|// len() over an ASCII-only grammar where bytes and runes\n33|// coincide, so no row can separate them; that is stated here,\n34|// not hidden. Every other string bound in the census scope flows\n35|// through the single measure helper of its package (census\n36|// ledger: StringLength, runeLength, stringLength), and the rune\n37|// rows pin the helper verdicts at one crossing member per\n38|// facade plus every provhost rune site.\n39|\n40|// validSpawnJSON is one valid Provider SpawnPlan body with the\n41|// given profile mapping, first extra argv element, literal value,\n42|// and native session ID literal. The argv always carries one\n43|// short flag so element-count rules hold while one member under\n44|// test varies.\n45|func validSpawnJSON(mapping, extraArgv, literalValue, nativeID string) []byte {\n46|\targv := `[\"--serve\"]`\n47|\tif extraArgv != \"\" {\n48|\t\targv = fmt.Sprintf(`[\"--serve\",%s]`, jsonQuote(extraArgv))\n49|\t}\n50|\tliterals := `{}`\n51|\tif literalValue != \"\" {\n52|\t\tliterals = fmt.Sprintf(`{\"EXTRA_KEY\":%s}`, jsonQuote(literalValue))\n53|\t}\n54|\tnative := `null`\n55|\tif nativeID != \"\" {\n56|\t\tnative = jsonQuote(nativeID)\n57|\t}\n58|\treturn []byte(fmt.Sprintf(`{\"argv\":%s,\"cwd\":\"/tmp/ax\",\"env_names\":[],\"env_literals\":%s,\"native_session_id\":%s,\"profile_mapping\":%s,\"extensions\":{}}`,\n59|\t\targv, literals, native, jsonQuote(mapping)))\n60|}\n61|\n62|// validSpawnMapping returns the production YOLO flag for codex:\n63|// scaffolding for rows whose probe point is a different member,\n64|// so a mapping change cannot break them for the wrong reason.\n65|// Rows whose probe point IS the mapping construct their own\n66|// lengths and never call this.\n67|func validSpawnMapping(t *testing.T) string {\n68|\tt.Helper()\n69|\tmapping, err := provhost.ProfileMapping(\"codex\", provhost.ProfileYOLO)\n70|\tif err != nil {\n71|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"scaffolding: %v\", err)\n72|\t}\n73|\treturn mapping\n74|}\n75|\n76|// jsonQuote quotes a Go string as a JSON string literal.\n77|func jsonQuote(value string) string {\n78|\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"%q\", value)\n79|}\n80|\n81|// TestStringMeasureCountsRunes proves the character measure at\n82|// the unit helper and at one crossing member per facade. Each\n83|// accept vector carries more bytes than its bound, so a\n84|// byte-measure would refuse it; each refuse vector carries one\n85|// character too many, so a widened bound would admit it.\n86|func TestStringMeasureCountsRunes(t *testing.T) {\n87|\tascii128 := strings.Repeat(\"v\", 128)\n88|\twide128 := strings.Repeat(\"é\", 128)\n89|\twide129 := strings.Repeat(\"é\", 129)\n90|\twide512 := strings.Repeat(\"é\", 512)\n91|\twide513 := strings.Repeat(\"é\", 513)\n92|\twide1024 := strings.Repeat(\"é\", 1024)\n93|\twide1025 := strings.Repeat(\"é\", 1025)\n94|\twide4096 := strings.Repeat(\"é\", 4096)\n95|\twide4097 := strings.Repeat(\"é\", 4097)\n96|\tt.Run(\"environ helper\", func(t *testing.T) {\n97|\t\tif _, ok := CheckStringBounds([]byte(jsonQuote(wide128)), 1, 128); !ok {\n98|\t\t\tt.Fatal(\"CheckStringBounds refused 128 characters in 256 bytes\")\n99|\t\t}\n100|\t\tif _, ok := CheckStringBounds([]byte(jsonQuote(wide129)), 1, 128); ok {\n101|\t\t\tt.Fatal(\"CheckStringBounds admitted 129 characters\")\n102|\t\t}\n103|\t\tif _, ok := CheckStringBounds([]byte(jsonQuote(ascii128)), 1, 128); !ok {\n104|\t\t\tt.Fatal(\"CheckStringBounds refused 128 ASCII characters\")\n105|\t\t}\n106|\t})\n107|\tt.Run(\"sessadapter tuple version\", func(t *testing.T) {\n108|\t\taccept := []byte(strings.Replace(validTupleJSON(), `\"2.1.0\"`, jsonQuote(wide128), 1))\n109|\t\tif _, err := sessadapter.DecodeTuple(accept); err != nil {\n110|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"DecodeTuple refused 128-character version: %v\", err)\n111|\t\t}\n112|\t\trefuse := []byte(strings.Replace(validTupleJSON(), `\"2.1.0\"`, jsonQuote(wide129), 1))\n113|\t\t_, err := sessadapter.DecodeTuple(refuse)\n114|\t\tif err == nil {\n115|\t\t\tt.Fatal(\"DecodeTuple admitted 129-character version\")\n116|\t\t}\n117|\t\tif !strings.Contains(err.Error(), \"string[1..128]\") {\n118|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"DecodeTuple error = %v, want the version bound arm\", err)\n119|\t\t}\n120|\t})\n121|\tt.Run(\"dirnode scan cursor\", func(t *testing.T) {\n122|\t\tif _, err := dirnode.CheckScanRequest(validScanRequestJSON(jsonQuote(wide4096))); err != nil {\n123|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"CheckScanRequest refused 4096-character cursor: %v\", err)\n124|\t\t}\n125|\t\t_, err := dirnode.CheckScanRequest(validScanRequestJSON(jsonQuote(wide4097)))\n126|\t\tif err == nil {\n127|\t\t\tt.Fatal(\"CheckScanRequest admitted 4097-character cursor\")\n128|\t\t}\n129|\t\tif !strings.Contains(err.Error(), \"string[1..4096]\") {\n130|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"CheckScanRequest error = %v, want the cursor bound arm\", err)\n131|\t\t}\n132|\t})\n133|\tt.Run(\"provhost profile mapping bound arm\", func(t *testing.T) {\n134|\t\tbound := validSpawnJSON(strings.Repeat(\"m\", 513), \"\", \"\", \"\")\n135|\t\terr := provhost.DecodeSpawnPlan(bound, \"codex\", provhost.ProfileYOLO, scalar.PlatformLinux)\n136|\t\tif err == nil {\n137|\t\t\tt.Fatal(\"DecodeSpawnPlan admitted 513-character mapping\")\n138|\t\t}\n139|\t\tif !strings.Contains(err.Error(), \"not at most 512 characters\") {\n140|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"DecodeSpawnPlan error = %v, want the mapping bound arm\", err)\n141|\t\t}\n142|\t})\n143|\tt.Run(\"provhost mapping admits 300 wide characters\", func(t *testing.T) {\n144|\t\t// 300 `é` is 300 characters but 600 bytes: the bound\n145|\t\t// arm must admit it (runes) and the equality arm must\n146|\t\t// refuse it (it is not the provider mapping). A byte\n147|\t\t// measure would fire the bound arm instead.\n148|\t\twide := validSpawnJSON(strings.Repeat(\"é\", 300), \"\", \"\", \"\")\n149|\t\terr := provhost.DecodeSpawnPlan(wide, \"codex\", provhost.ProfileYOLO, scalar.PlatformLinux)\n150|\t\tif err == nil {\n151|\t\t\tt.Fatal(\"DecodeSpawnPlan admitted a mapping that is not the provider mapping\")\n152|\t\t}\n153|\t\tif !strings.Contains(err.Error(), \"does not match the provider profile\") {\n154|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"DecodeSpawnPlan error = %v, want the mapping equality arm, not the bound arm\", err)\n155|\t\t}\n156|\t})\n157|\tt.Run(\"provhost native session id bound\", func(t *testing.T) {\n158|\t\tmapping := validSpawnMapping(t)\n159|\t\taccept := validSpawnJSON(mapping, \"\", \"\", wide512)\n160|\t\tif err := provhost.DecodeSpawnPlan(accept, \"codex\", provhost.ProfileYOLO, scalar.PlatformLinux); err != nil {\n161|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"DecodeSpawnPlan refused 512-character native session id: %v\", err)\n162|\t\t}\n163|\t\trefuse := validSpawnJSON(mapping, \"\", \"\", wide513)\n164|\t\terr := provhost.DecodeSpawnPlan(refuse, \"codex\", provhost.ProfileYOLO, scalar.PlatformLinux)\n165|\t\tif err == nil {\n166|\t\t\tt.Fatal(\"DecodeSpawnPlan admitted 513-character native session id\")\n167|\t\t}\n168|\t\tif !strings.Contains(err.Error(), \"1..512 characters\") {\n169|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"DecodeSpawnPlan error = %v, want the native session id bound arm\", err)\n170|\t\t}\n171|\t})\n172|\tt.Run(\"identity opaque bound agrees\", func(t *testing.T) {\n173|\t\t// The opaque_identity value bound (1..1024 runes) is\n174|\t\t// the one member validated by both identity dialects:\n175|\t\t// both judges must agree on the multibyte edges.\n176|\t\taccept := mutateMember(t, validIdentityJSON(), \"opaque_identity\", `{\"k\":`+jsonQuote(wide1024)+`}`)\n177|\t\tif err := provhost.CheckIdentity(accept, \"antigravity\"); err != nil {\n178|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"CheckIdentity refused 1024-character opaque value: %v\", err)\n179|\t\t}\n180|\t\tif _, _, err := canonicaljson.CalculateObjectIdentity(accept); err != nil {\n181|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"CalculateObjectIdentity refused 1024-character opaque value: %v\", err)\n182|\t\t}\n183|\t\trefuse := mutateMember(t, validIdentityJSON(), \"opaque_identity\", `{\"k\":`+jsonQuote(wide1025)+`}`)\n184|\t\tif err := provhost.CheckIdentity(refuse, \"antigravity\"); err == nil {\n185|\t\t\tt.Fatal(\"CheckIdentity admitted 1025-character opaque value\")\n186|\t\t}\n187|\t\tif _, _, err := canonicaljson.CalculateObjectIdentity(refuse); err == nil {\n188|\t\t\tt.Fatal(\"CalculateObjectIdentity admitted 1025-character opaque value\")\n189|\t\t}\n190|\t})\n191|}\n192|\n193|// TestByteBoundsStayBytes proves the three ledgered byte gates\n194|// keep measuring bytes: each vector is within the rune bound a\n195|// character measure would enforce but over the byte bound the\n196|// specification states, so a rune-measure regression would admit\n197|// it and travel to a later arm instead of the byte arm.\n198|func TestByteBoundsStayBytes(t *testing.T) {\n199|\tmapping := validSpawnMapping(t)\n200|\tt.Run(\"argv element bytes\", func(t *testing.T) {\n201|\t\t// 2049 `é` is 2049 characters but 4098 bytes.\n202|\t\tbody := validSpawnJSON(mapping, strings.Repeat(\"é\", 2049), \"\", \"\")\n203|\t\terr := provhost.DecodeSpawnPlan(body, \"codex\", provhost.ProfileYOLO, scalar.PlatformLinux)\n204|\t\tif err == nil {\n205|\t\t\tt.Fatal(\"DecodeSpawnPlan admitted a 4098-byte argv element\")\n206|\t\t}\n207|\t\tif !strings.Contains(err.Error(), \"NUL-free bytes\") {\n208|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"DecodeSpawnPlan error = %v, want the argv element byte arm\", err)\n209|\t\t}\n210|\t})\n211|\tt.Run(\"argv total bytes\", func(t *testing.T) {\n212|\t\t// Seventeen 4000-byte elements pass the element gate\n213|\t\t// and fail the 65536-byte total.\n214|\t\telements := make([]string, 0, 17)\n215|\t\tfor index := 0; index < 17; index++ {\n216|\t\t\telements = append(elements, jsonQuote(strings.Repeat(\"a\", 4000)))\n217|\t\t}\n218|\t\tbody := []byte(fmt.Sprintf(`{\"argv\":[\"--serve\",%s],\"cwd\":\"/tmp/ax\",\"env_names\":[],\"env_literals\":{},\"native_session_id\":null,\"profile_mapping\":%s,\"extensions\":{}}`,\n219|\t\t\tstrings.Join(elements, \",\"), jsonQuote(mapping)))\n220|\t\terr := provhost.DecodeSpawnPlan(body, \"codex\", provhost.ProfileYOLO, scalar.PlatformLinux)\n221|\t\tif err == nil {\n222|\t\t\tt.Fatal(\"DecodeSpawnPlan admitted argv over 65536 total bytes\")\n223|\t\t}\n224|\t\tif !strings.Contains(err.Error(), \"65536 bytes total\") {\n225|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"DecodeSpawnPlan error = %v, want the argv total byte arm\", err)\n226|\t\t}\n227|\t})\n228|\tt.Run(\"env literal bytes\", func(t *testing.T) {\n229|\t\tbody := validSpawnJSON(mapping, \"\", strings.Repeat(\"é\", 2049), \"\")\n230|\t\terr := provhost.DecodeSpawnPlan(body, \"codex\", provhost.ProfileYOLO, scalar.PlatformLinux)\n231|\t\tif err == nil {\n232|\t\t\tt.Fatal(\"DecodeSpawnPlan admitted a 4098-byte env literal\")\n233|\t\t}\n234|\t\tif !strings.Contains(err.Error(), \"4096 NUL-free bytes\") {\n235|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"DecodeSpawnPlan error = %v, want the env literal byte arm\", err)\n236|\t\t}\n237|\t})\n238|}"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c623","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07664-b32a-7b03-be28-978067559ac9"},"sequence":364,"recorded_at":1780531400000723,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"4279c805-073c-4405-a747-7b1a47e438ac","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"4279c805-073c-4405-a747-7b1a47e438ac","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"4279c805-073c-4405-a747-7b1a47e438ac"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"08a74324-625a-40a3-a5b8-fa7e58c8c530"},"task_id":"08a74324-625a-40a3-a5b8-fa7e58c8c530","event":{"kind":"completed","task_id":"08a74324-625a-40a3-a5b8-fa7e58c8c530"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c625","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07664-b32a-7b03-be28-978067559ac9"},"sequence":365,"recorded_at":1780531400000725,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"4279c805-073c-4405-a747-7b1a47e438ac","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"4279c805-073c-4405-a747-7b1a47e438ac","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"4279c805-073c-4405-a747-7b1a47e438ac"},"call_id":"call_01a07665c58d70e3911435aac99d15ae","text":"Read text file `internal/provhost/surrogate.go`.\n1|package provhost\n2|\n3|// This file is the local lone-surrogate gate for the Section 1.6 wire\n4|// bodies this package decodes. Pinned specification Section 1.6 requires\n5|// decoders to reject lone surrogate code points before canonicalization,\n6|// and the repository already enforces that rule in\n7|// internal/canonicaljson (validateSurrogateEscapes, called from\n8|// decodeStrict). This package decodes with its own strict object reader\n9|// (decodeStrictObject in protocol.go) because it must keep member-level\n10|// fault attribution (duplicate member names, the offending member) that\n11|// the shared decoder does not report, and encoding/json silently replaces\n12|// a lone \\ud800-style escape with U+FFFD instead of failing. So the gate\n13|// lives here, scans the raw frame bytes before decoding, and refuses the\n14|// same class the shared package refuses.\n15|//\n16|// The gate is deliberately a copy, not an import: internal/canonicaljson\n17|// is byte-identical shared baseline text that two unlanded stories must\n18|// not edit at once, so neither story may add an export there. The\n19|// surrogate-vector sweep in surrogate_test.go drives both this gate\n20|// (through decodeStrictObject) and canonicaljson.Canonicalize over a\n21|// derived enumeration of the code-point space, so the copies cannot\n22|// drift silently: a divergence reddens there rather than passing\n23|// unnoticed. The sweep judges verdicts against the independent\n24|// implementation, never against a shared hand-written expectation.\n25|//\n26|// The gate decides the surrogate-escape question only. Malformed\n27|// escapes and unterminated strings are not its verdict: they fall\n28|// through to the JSON-syntax arms that already own them. Non-UTF-8\n29|// bytes never reach it: decodeStrictObject refuses them first,\n30|// because a raw WTF-8 surrogate encoding would otherwise slip past\n31|// this escape scanner and be silently replaced with U+FFFD by\n32|// encoding/json. A lone high surrogate is a high unit not immediately\n33|// followed by a \\uDC00–\\uDFFF escape; a lone low surrogate is a low\n34|// unit in any other position. Both are refused before any member is\n35|// read.\n36|\n37|// The gate's own range constants: the high and low surrogate halves\n38|// of the Section 1.6 verdict space. The\n39|// surrogate-vector sweep in surrogate_test.go derives its pair-second\n40|// dimension from these constants arithmetically (bounds plus and minus\n41|// small offsets), so the boundary neighborhood is enumerated from the\n42|// gate rather than from a hand-written literal: shifting a bound here\n43|// moves the swept neighborhood with it instead of silently uncovering\n44|// it. Verdicts still come from the independent implementation, never\n45|// from these constants, so a wrong bound reddens against the oracle.\n46|const (\n47|\thighSurrogateMin = 0xd800\n48|\thighSurrogateMax = 0xdbff\n49|\tlowSurrogateMin  = 0xdc00\n50|\tlowSurrogateMax  = 0xdfff\n51|)\n52|\n53|// hasLoneSurrogateEscape reports whether raw JSON bytes carry a lone\n54|// surrogate escape inside any string. The string walk mirrors the shared\n55|// package's walker (backslash handling included: a \\\\ escape consumes\n56|// both bytes, so the text \"\\\\ud800\" is backslash-plus-text, not an\n57|// escape), but only the surrogate verdict is returned.\n58|func hasLoneSurrogateEscape(input []byte) bool {\n59|\tfor index := 0; index < len(input); index++ {\n60|\t\tif input[index] != '\"' {\n61|\t\t\tcontinue\n62|\t\t}\n63|\t\tfor index++; index < len(input); index++ {\n64|\t\t\tif input[index] == '\"' {\n65|\t\t\t\tgoto stringComplete\n66|\t\t\t}\n67|\t\t\tif input[index] != '\\\\' {\n68|\t\t\t\tcontinue\n69|\t\t\t}\n70|\t\t\tindex++\n71|\t\t\tif index >= len(input) || input[index] != 'u' {\n72|\t\t\t\tcontinue\n73|\t\t\t}\n74|\t\t\tunit, end, ok := readHexUnit(input, index-1)\n75|\t\t\tif !ok {\n76|\t\t\t\t// Not a well-formed \\uXXXX escape: the\n77|\t\t\t\t// JSON-syntax arms own it, not this gate.\n78|\t\t\t\tcontinue\n79|\t\t\t}\n80|\t\t\tindex = end - 1\n81|\t\t\tif unit >= highSurrogateMin && unit <= highSurrogateMax {\n82|\t\t\t\tlow, lowEnd, ok := readHexUnit(input, end)\n83|\t\t\t\tif !ok || low < lowSurrogateMin || low > lowSurrogateMax {\n84|\t\t\t\t\treturn true\n85|\t\t\t\t}\n86|\t\t\t\tindex = lowEnd - 1\n87|\t\t\t} else if unit >= lowSurrogateMin && unit <= lowSurrogateMax {\n88|\t\t\t\treturn true\n89|\t\t\t}\n90|\t\t}\n91|\t\t// The string never closed: malformed JSON the syntax arms\n92|\t\t// refuse, so the gate claims no surrogate verdict here.\n93|\t\treturn false\n94|\tstringComplete:\n95|\t}\n96|\treturn false\n97|}\n98|\n99|// readHexUnit parses one \\uXXXX escape at input[start]. It reports false\n100|// when the bytes are not a well-formed escape; hex digits parse in\n101|// either case, matching the shared package's ParseUint base-16 read.\n102|func readHexUnit(input []byte, start int) (uint16, int, bool) {\n103|\tif start < 0 || start+6 > len(input) || input[start] != '\\\\' || input[start+1] != 'u' {\n104|\t\treturn 0, start, false\n105|\t}\n106|\tvar value uint16\n107|\tfor _, b := range input[start+2 : start+6] {\n108|\t\tvar digit byte\n109|\t\tif b >= '0' && b <= '9' {\n110|\t\t\tdigit = b - '0'\n111|\t\t} else if b >= 'a' && b <= 'f' {\n112|\t\t\tdigit = b - 'a' + 10\n113|\t\t} else if b >= 'A' && b <= 'F' {\n114|\t\t\tdigit = b - 'A' + 10\n115|\t\t} else {\n116|\t\t\treturn 0, start, false\n117|\t\t}\n118|\t\tvalue = value*16 + uint16(digit)\n119|\t}\n120|\treturn value, start + 6, true\n121|}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c627","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07664-b32a-7b03-be28-978067559ac9"},"sequence":366,"recorded_at":1780531400000727,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"4279c805-073c-4405-a747-7b1a47e438ac","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"4279c805-073c-4405-a747-7b1a47e438ac","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"4279c805-073c-4405-a747-7b1a47e438ac"},"call_id":"call_01a07665c62e73439a97b6887d0f2b6e","text":"Read text file `internal/environ/observation_test.go`.\n1|package environ\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"reflect\"\n5|\t\"sort\"\n6|\t\"strings\"\n7|\t\"testing\"\n8|\n9|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/scalar\"\n10|)\n11|\n12|// This file batteries the Section 10.8.1 Environment\n13|// Observation gate. No facade validates observation content\n14|// today — dirnode crosses observations as presence and object\n15|// shape only, explicitly deferring content to this leaf — so\n16|// these rows prove new behavior, not agreement. The roster is\n17|// still derived and fail-closed: the required-member list comes\n18|// from environ production, every required member owns at least\n19|// one refusal row, and a row naming a member production no\n20|// longer requires fails as orphaned.\n21|//\n22|// Conjoined rules count twice throughout: sorted-unique evidence\n23|// owns an unsorted-but-unique row AND a sorted-but-duplicated\n24|// row, and reason coherence owns an available-with-reason row\n25|// AND a conditional-without-reason row, so a check enforcing\n26|// only one half cannot pass both.\n27|\n28|// observationRow is one battery vector: the required member it\n29|// violates (\"\" for vocabulary and structural rules), the body,\n30|// and the rule phrase the refusal must carry. An empty phrase\n31|// means the entry accepts and the decoded value is asserted.\n32|type observationRow struct {\n33|\tmember string\n34|\tname   string\n35|\tbody   []byte\n36|\ttext   string\n37|}\n38|\n39|// capabilityValueJSON builds one CapabilityResult with the given\n40|// status, reason literal (already JSON), and evidence literal.\n41|func capabilityValueJSON(status, reason, evidence string) string {\n42|\treturn `{\"status\":` + jsonQuote(status) + `,\"reason_code\":` + reason + `,\"evidence_ids\":` + evidence + `,\"observed_at\":` + jsonQuote(fixtureObservedAt) + `,\"extensions\":{}}`\n43|}\n44|\n45|// observationCorpus mutates each observation member alone\n46|// against an otherwise-valid body.\n47|func observationCorpus(t *testing.T) []observationRow {\n48|\tt.Helper()\n49|\tvalid := validObservationJSON()\n50|\tdrop := func(member string) []byte { return dropMember(t, valid, member) }\n51|\tset := func(member, literal string) []byte { return mutateMember(t, valid, member, literal) }\n52|\tevidencePair := sortedDigests(fixtureEvidenceID, fixtureExecutable)\n53|\tunsortedEvidence := `[\"` + evidencePair[1] + `\",\"` + evidencePair[0] + `\"]`\n54|\tduplicatedEvidence := `[\"` + evidencePair[0] + `\",\"` + evidencePair[0] + `\"]`\n55|\tcapWith := func(status, reason, evidence string) []byte {\n56|\t\tcapabilities := strings.Replace(validCapabilitiesJSON(), availableCapabilityJSON(), capabilityValueJSON(status, reason, evidence), 1)\n57|\t\treturn mutateMember(t, valid, \"capabilities\", capabilities)\n58|\t}\n59|\tsevenCaps := sevenCapabilitiesJSON(t)\n60|\treturn []observationRow{\n61|\t\t{\"\", \"valid\", valid, \"\"},\n62|\t\t{\"schema\", \"missing schema\", drop(\"schema\"), \"misses a required member\"},\n63|\t\t{\"schema\", \"wrong schema\", set(\"schema\", `\"urn:ax:schema:session-adapter-manifest\"`), \"not the environment observation\"},\n64|\t\t{\"schema_version\", \"wrong version\", set(\"schema_version\", `\"2.0.0\"`), \"not 1.0.0\"},\n65|\t\t{\"observation_id\", \"bad observation digest\", set(\"observation_id\", `\"sha256:zzzz\"`), \"not a digest\"},\n66|\t\t{\"host_id\", \"bad host uuid\", set(\"host_id\", `\"not-a-uuid\"`), \"not a UUIDv7\"},\n67|\t\t{\"installation_id\", \"bad installation digest\", set(\"installation_id\", `\"42\"`), \"not a digest\"},\n68|\t\t{\"environment_id\", \"bad environment id\", set(\"environment_id\", `\"Test.Env\"`), \"environment-id\"},\n69|\t\t{\"environment_id\", \"missing environment id\", drop(\"environment_id\"), \"misses a required member\"},\n70|\t\t{\"environment_version\", \"empty version\", set(\"environment_version\", `\"\"`), \"string[1..128]\"},\n71|\t\t{\"environment_version\", \"long version\", set(\"environment_version\", jsonQuote(strings.Repeat(\"v\", 129))), \"string[1..128]\"},\n72|\t\t{\"provider_id\", \"uppercase provider\", set(\"provider_id\", `\"Test-Provider\"`), \"provider-id\"},\n73|\t\t{\"platform\", \"darwin refused\", set(\"platform\", `\"darwin\"`), \"platform\"},\n74|\t\t{\"platform\", \"wsl2 admits\", set(\"platform\", `\"wsl2\"`), \"\"},\n75|\t\t{\"architecture\", \"x86 refused\", set(\"architecture\", `\"x86\"`), \"architecture\"},\n76|\t\t{\"backend_realm_fingerprint\", \"bad realm digest\", set(\"backend_realm_fingerprint\", `\"null\"`), \"not a digest\"},\n77|\t\t{\"capabilities\", \"seven capabilities refused\", set(\"capabilities\", sevenCaps), \"exact eight-name\"},\n78|\t\t{\"capabilities\", \"ninth capability refused\", set(\"capabilities\", nineCapabilitiesJSON(t)), \"exact eight-name\"},\n79|\t\t{\"capabilities\", \"ninth capability refused\", appendMember(t, valid, \"capabilities-extra\", `{}`), \"unknown member\"},\n80|\t\t{\"capabilities\", \"unknown capability key\", set(\"capabilities\", unknownCapabilityJSON(t)), \"exact eight-name\"},\n81|\t\t{\"capabilities\", \"bad status refused\", capWith(\"ready\", `null`, `[]`), \"exact eight-name\"},\n82|\t\t{\"capabilities\", \"available with reason refused\", capWith(\"available\", jsonQuote(\"why\"), `[]`), \"exact eight-name\"},\n83|\t\t{\"capabilities\", \"conditional without reason refused\", capWith(\"conditional\", `null`, `[]`), \"exact eight-name\"},\n84|\t\t{\"capabilities\", \"conditional with reason admits\", capWith(\"conditional\", jsonQuote(\"why\"), `[]`), \"\"},\n85|\t\t{\"capabilities\", \"unsorted evidence refused\", capWith(\"available\", `null`, unsortedEvidence), \"exact eight-name\"},\n86|\t\t{\"capabilities\", \"duplicated evidence refused\", capWith(\"available\", `null`, duplicatedEvidence), \"exact eight-name\"},\n87|\t\t{\"capabilities\", \"bad evidence digest refused\", capWith(\"available\", `null`, `[\"sha256:zzzz\"]`), \"exact eight-name\"},\n88|\t\t{\"authentication_status\", \"bad auth status\", set(\"authentication_status\", `\"signed-in\"`), \"authentication status\"},\n89|\t\t{\"runtime_status\", \"bad runtime status\", set(\"runtime_status\", `\"sleeping\"`), \"runtime status\"},\n90|\t\t{\"observed_at\", \"bad timestamp\", set(\"observed_at\", `\"yesterday\"`), \"not a timestamp\"},\n91|\t\t{\"observed_at\", \"missing timestamp\", drop(\"observed_at\"), \"misses a required member\"},\n92|\t\t{\"extensions\", \"bad extensions key\", set(\"extensions\", `{\"nodots\":1}`), \"reverse-DNS\"},\n93|\t\t{\"\", \"unknown top member\", appendMember(t, valid, \"score\", `1`), \"unknown member\"},\n94|\t}\n95|}\n96|\n97|// sortedDigests returns two distinct fixture digests in JCS\n98|// (lexicographic) order.\n99|func sortedDigests(first, second string) []string {\n100|\tpair := []string{first, second}\n101|\tsort.Strings(pair)\n102|\tif pair[0] == pair[1] {\n103|\t\tpanic(\"sortedDigests: fixtures collide\")\n104|\t}\n105|\treturn pair\n106|}\n107|\n108|// sevenCapabilitiesJSON returns the capability map without its\n109|// first registry name.\n110|func sevenCapabilitiesJSON(t *testing.T) string {\n111|\tt.Helper()\n112|\tfull := validCapabilitiesJSON()\n113|\twithout := strings.Replace(full, `\"directory_discovery\":`+availableCapabilityJSON()+`,`, \"\", 1)\n114|\tif without == full {\n115|\t\tt.Fatal(\"sevenCapabilitiesJSON: anchor not found\")\n116|\t}\n117|\treturn without\n118|}\n119|\n120|// nineCapabilitiesJSON returns the capability map with a ninth\n121|// valid-valued key: the length arm, distinct from the unknown-key\n122|// arm the swap below exercises.\n123|func nineCapabilitiesJSON(t *testing.T) string {\n124|\tt.Helper()\n125|\tfull := validCapabilitiesJSON()\n126|\tnine := strings.Replace(full, `\"native_resume\":`, `\"extra_surface\":`+availableCapabilityJSON()+`,\"native_resume\":`, 1)\n127|\tif nine == full {\n128|\t\tt.Fatal(\"nineCapabilitiesJSON: anchor not found\")\n129|\t}\n130|\treturn nine\n131|}\n132|\n133|// unknownCapabilityJSON returns the eight-name map with one key\n134|// swapped for an unregistered name.\n135|func unknownCapabilityJSON(t *testing.T) string {\n136|\tt.Helper()\n137|\tfull := validCapabilitiesJSON()\n138|\tswapped := strings.Replace(full, `\"directory_discovery\"`, `\"directory_exploration\"`, 1)\n139|\tif swapped == full {\n140|\t\tt.Fatal(\"unknownCapabilityJSON: anchor not found\")\n141|\t}\n142|\treturn swapped\n143|}\n144|\n145|// TestObservationRosterIsClosed requires every derived required\n146|// member to own at least one row, and every row to name a\n147|// derived member (or \"\" for vocabulary and structural rules).\n148|func TestObservationRosterIsClosed(t *testing.T) {\n149|\trequired := deriveRequiredList(t, \"environ\", \"observation.go\", \"observationRequired\")\n150|\tderived := map[string]bool{}\n151|\tfor _, member := range required {\n152|\t\tderived[member] = true\n153|\t}\n154|\tcovered := map[string]bool{}\n155|\tfor _, row := range observationCorpus(t) {\n156|\t\tif row.member == \"\" {\n157|\t\t\tcontinue\n158|\t\t}\n159|\t\tif !derived[row.member] {\n160|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"row %q names underived member %q\", row.name, row.member)\n161|\t\t}\n162|\t\tcovered[row.member] = true\n163|\t}\n164|\tfor _, member := range required {\n165|\t\tif !covered[member] {\n166|\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"derived required member %q owns no battery row\", member)\n167|\t\t}\n168|\t}\n169|}\n170|\n171|// TestDecodeEnvironmentObservation drives the corpus through the\n172|// production entry: accepts decode to the fixture values, and\n173|// every refusal carries its full rule rendering.\n174|func TestDecodeEnvironmentObservation(t *testing.T) {\n175|\tfor _, row := range observationCorpus(t) {\n176|\t\tt.Run(row.name, func(t *testing.T) {\n177|\t\t\tobservation, err := DecodeEnvironmentObservation(row.body)\n178|\t\t\tif row.text == \"\" {\n179|\t\t\t\tif err != nil {\n180|\t\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"refused %s: %v\", row.body, err)\n181|\t\t\t\t}\n182|\t\t\t\tassertObservationFixture(t, observation)\n183|\t\t\t\treturn\n184|\t\t\t}\n185|\t\t\tif err == nil {\n186|\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"admitted %s, want rule %q\", row.body, row.text)\n187|\t\t\t}\n188|\t\t\tif !strings.Contains(err.Error(), row.text) {\n189|\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"error = %v, want rule %q\", err, row.text)\n190|\t\t\t}\n191|\t\t})\n192|\t}\n193|}\n194|\n195|// assertObservationFixture requires the decoded accept to carry\n196|// the shared fixture identities: the verdict is accept AND the\n197|// values are the fixture's, so a decoder that accepts while\n198|// misreading a member cannot pass.\n199|func assertObservationFixture(t *testing.T, observation Observation) {\n200|\tt.Helper()\n201|\tif observation.ObservationID != fixtureObserveID {\n202|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"observation id = %q, want %q\", observation.ObservationID, fixtureObserveID)\n203|\t}\n204|\tif observation.HostID != fixtureHostID {\n205|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"host id = %q, want %q\", observation.HostID, fixtureHostID)\n206|\t}\n207|\tif observation.InstallationID != fixtureInstallID {\n208|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"installation id = %q, want %q\", observation.InstallationID, fixtureInstallID)\n209|\t}\n210|\tif observation.EnvironmentID != fixtureEnvironmentID {\n211|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"environment id = %q, want %q\", observation.EnvironmentID, fixtureEnvironmentID)\n212|\t}\n213|\tif observation.ProviderID != fixtureProviderID {\n214|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"provider id = %q, want %q\", observation.ProviderID, fixtureProviderID)\n215|\t}\n216|\tif len(observation.Capabilities) != 8 {\n217|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"capabilities = %d entries, want the exact eight\", len(observation.Capabilities))\n218|\t}\n219|}\n220|\n221|// TestDirectoryCapabilityTableIsShared requires the environ and\n222|// dirnode directory-capability tables to be literally equal. The\n223|// adapter fifteen-name and provider seven-name tables share the\n224|// symbol name but are different rules in different stories, so\n225|// they are out of scope here by rule identity, not by silence:\n226|// this comparison names its files.\n227|func TestDirectoryCapabilityTableIsShared(t *testing.T) {\n228|\tmine := deriveRequiredList(t, \"environ\", \"observation.go\", \"capabilityOrder\")\n229|\ttheirs := deriveRequiredList(t, \"dirnode\", \"manifest.go\", \"capabilityOrder\")\n230|\tif !reflect.DeepEqual(mine, theirs) {\n231|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"directory capability tables differ:\\nenviron: %q\\ndirnode:  %q\", mine, theirs)\n232|\t}\n233|\tif len(mine) != 8 {\n234|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"directory capability table has %d names, want the exact eight\", len(mine))\n235|\t}\n236|}\n237|\n238|// TestArchitectureTableIsShared requires the three architecture\n239|// tables in scope to be literally equal.\n240|func TestArchitectureTableIsShared(t *testing.T) {\n241|\tmine := deriveRequiredList(t, \"environ\", \"tuple.go\", \"tupleArchitectures\")\n242|\tadapter := deriveRequiredList(t, \"sessadapter\", \"tuple.go\", \"tupleArchitectures\")\n243|\tnode := deriveRequiredList(t, \"dirnode\", \"probe.go\", \"architectures\")\n244|\tif !reflect.DeepEqual(mine, adapter) || !reflect.DeepEqual(mine, node) {\n245|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"architecture tables differ:\\nenviron: %q\\nsessadapter: %q\\ndirnode: %q\", mine, adapter, node)\n246|\t}\n247|}\n248|\n249|// TestNegotiatedPlatformsParse requires every platform token in\n250|// the derived dirnode v2 vocabulary to parse as a scalar\n251|// platform, and requires the legacy v1 darwin token to refuse:\n252|// the vocabularies are per-major by design, and a token that\n253|// crossed majors silently would break the Section 7.9 binding.\n254|func TestNegotiatedPlatformsParse(t *testing.T) {\n255|\tv2 := deriveRequiredList(t, \"dirnode\", \"probe.go\", \"platformV2\")\n256|\tif len(v2) != 4 {\n257|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"platformV2 has %d tokens, want four\", len(v2))\n258|\t}\n259|\tfor _, token := range v2 {\n260|\t\tif _, err := scalar.ParsePlatform(token); err != nil {\n261|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"v2 token %q does not parse as a platform: %v\", token, err)\n262|\t\t}\n263|\t}\n264|\tif _, err := scalar.ParsePlatform(\"darwin\"); err == nil {\n265|\t\tt.Fatal(\"legacy darwin parses as a platform; the majors are no longer separated\")\n266|\t}\n267|}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c629","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07664-b32a-7b03-be28-978067559ac9"},"sequence":367,"recorded_at":1780531400000729,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"4279c805-073c-4405-a747-7b1a47e438ac","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"4279c805-073c-4405-a747-7b1a47e438ac","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"4279c805-073c-4405-a747-7b1a47e438ac"},"call_id":"call_01a07665c6ed7043867f7c0daf4a1495","text":"Read text file `internal/environ/measure_agreement_test.go`.\n1|package environ\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"fmt\"\n5|\t\"strings\"\n6|\t\"testing\"\n7|\n8|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/canonicaljson\"\n9|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/dirnode\"\n10|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/provhost\"\n11|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/scalar\"\n12|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/sessadapter\"\n13|)\n14|\n15|// This file is the cross-facade string-measure battery. Section\n16|// 1.6 bounds strings in characters, not bytes: string[1..128]\n17|// admits 128 characters of any width. Two strict decoders both\n18|// blind to lone surrogates was one drift class the cross-story\n19|// review found; byte-vs-rune bounds disagreeing on a member that\n20|// crosses both protocols was another. This battery pins the\n21|// measure at every character-bound member one facade shares with\n22|// another, with multibyte vectors that separate the measures: a\n23|// 128-`é` value is 128 characters but 256 bytes, so a\n24|// byte-measure refuses what the specification admits.\n25|//\n26|// The byte side is ledgered, not left open. Provider SpawnPlan\n27|// argv elements and totals and env-literal values bound BYTES by\n28|// Section 5.1 (outside this story), implemented in exactly two\n29|// functions — provhost checkSpawnArgv and checkSpawnEnvLiterals\n30|// — and the byte rows below drive all three byte gates through\n31|// the production DecodeSpawnPlan entry. validEnvName measures\n32|// len() over an ASCII-only grammar where bytes and runes\n33|// coincide, so no row can separate them; that is stated here,\n34|// not hidden. Every other string bound in the census scope flows\n35|// through the single measure helper of its package (census\n36|// ledger: StringLength, runeLength, stringLength), and the rune\n37|// rows pin the helper verdicts at one crossing member per\n38|// facade plus every provhost rune site.\n39|\n40|// validSpawnJSON is one valid Provider SpawnPlan body with the\n41|// given profile mapping, first extra argv element, literal value,\n42|// and native session ID literal. The argv always carries one\n43|// short flag so element-count rules hold while one member under\n44|// test varies.\n45|func validSpawnJSON(mapping, extraArgv, literalValue, nativeID string) []byte {\n46|\targv := `[\"--serve\"]`\n47|\tif extraArgv != \"\" {\n48|\t\targv = fmt.Sprintf(`[\"--serve\",%s]`, jsonQuote(extraArgv))\n49|\t}\n50|\tliterals := `{}`\n51|\tif literalValue != \"\" {\n52|\t\tliterals = fmt.Sprintf(`{\"EXTRA_KEY\":%s}`, jsonQuote(literalValue))\n53|\t}\n54|\tnative := `null`\n55|\tif nativeID != \"\" {\n56|\t\tnative = jsonQuote(nativeID)\n57|\t}\n58|\treturn []byte(fmt.Sprintf(`{\"argv\":%s,\"cwd\":\"/tmp/ax\",\"env_names\":[],\"env_literals\":%s,\"native_session_id\":%s,\"profile_mapping\":%s,\"extensions\":{}}`,\n59|\t\targv, literals, native, jsonQuote(mapping)))\n60|}\n61|\n62|// validSpawnMapping returns the production YOLO flag for codex:\n63|// scaffolding for rows whose probe point is a different member,\n64|// so a mapping change cannot break them for the wrong reason.\n65|// Rows whose probe point IS the mapping construct their own\n66|// lengths and never call this.\n67|func validSpawnMapping(t *testing.T) string {\n68|\tt.Helper()\n69|\tmapping, err := provhost.ProfileMapping(\"codex\", provhost.ProfileYOLO)\n70|\tif err != nil {\n71|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"scaffolding: %v\", err)\n72|\t}\n73|\treturn mapping\n74|}\n75|\n76|// jsonQuote quotes a Go string as a JSON string literal.\n77|func jsonQuote(value string) string {\n78|\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"%q\", value)\n79|}\n80|\n81|// TestStringMeasureCountsRunes proves the character measure at\n82|// the unit helper and at one crossing member per facade. Each\n83|// accept vector carries more bytes than its bound, so a\n84|// byte-measure would refuse it; each refuse vector carries one\n85|// character too many, so a widened bound would admit it.\n86|func TestStringMeasureCountsRunes(t *testing.T) {\n87|\tascii128 := strings.Repeat(\"v\", 128)\n88|\twide128 := strings.Repeat(\"é\", 128)\n89|\twide129 := strings.Repeat(\"é\", 129)\n90|\twide512 := strings.Repeat(\"é\", 512)\n91|\twide513 := strings.Repeat(\"é\", 513)\n92|\twide1024 := strings.Repeat(\"é\", 1024)\n93|\twide1025 := strings.Repeat(\"é\", 1025)\n94|\twide4096 := strings.Repeat(\"é\", 4096)\n95|\twide4097 := strings.Repeat(\"é\", 4097)\n96|\tt.Run(\"environ helper\", func(t *testing.T) {\n97|\t\tif _, ok := CheckStringBounds([]byte(jsonQuote(wide128)), 1, 128); !ok {\n98|\t\t\tt.Fatal(\"CheckStringBounds refused 128 characters in 256 bytes\")\n99|\t\t}\n100|\t\tif _, ok := CheckStringBounds([]byte(jsonQuote(wide129)), 1, 128); ok {\n101|\t\t\tt.Fatal(\"CheckStringBounds admitted 129 characters\")\n102|\t\t}\n103|\t\tif _, ok := CheckStringBounds([]byte(jsonQuote(ascii128)), 1, 128); !ok {\n104|\t\t\tt.Fatal(\"CheckStringBounds refused 128 ASCII characters\")\n105|\t\t}\n106|\t})\n107|\tt.Run(\"sessadapter tuple version\", func(t *testing.T) {\n108|\t\taccept := []byte(strings.Replace(validTupleJSON(), `\"2.1.0\"`, jsonQuote(wide128), 1))\n109|\t\tif _, err := sessadapter.DecodeTuple(accept); err != nil {\n110|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"DecodeTuple refused 128-character version: %v\", err)\n111|\t\t}\n112|\t\trefuse := []byte(strings.Replace(validTupleJSON(), `\"2.1.0\"`, jsonQuote(wide129), 1))\n113|\t\t_, err := sessadapter.DecodeTuple(refuse)\n114|\t\tif err == nil {\n115|\t\t\tt.Fatal(\"DecodeTuple admitted 129-character version\")\n116|\t\t}\n117|\t\tif !strings.Contains(err.Error(), \"string[1..128]\") {\n118|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"DecodeTuple error = %v, want the version bound arm\", err)\n119|\t\t}\n120|\t})\n121|\tt.Run(\"dirnode scan cursor\", func(t *testing.T) {\n122|\t\tif _, err := dirnode.CheckScanRequest(validScanRequestJSON(jsonQuote(wide4096))); err != nil {\n123|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"CheckScanRequest refused 4096-character cursor: %v\", err)\n124|\t\t}\n125|\t\t_, err := dirnode.CheckScanRequest(validScanRequestJSON(jsonQuote(wide4097)))\n126|\t\tif err == nil {\n127|\t\t\tt.Fatal(\"CheckScanRequest admitted 4097-character cursor\")\n128|\t\t}\n129|\t\tif !strings.Contains(err.Error(), \"string[1..4096]\") {\n130|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"CheckScanRequest error = %v, want the cursor bound arm\", err)\n131|\t\t}\n132|\t})\n133|\tt.Run(\"provhost profile mapping bound arm\", func(t *testing.T) {\n134|\t\tbound := validSpawnJSON(strings.Repeat(\"m\", 513), \"\", \"\", \"\")\n135|\t\terr := provhost.DecodeSpawnPlan(bound, \"codex\", provhost.ProfileYOLO, scalar.PlatformLinux)\n136|\t\tif err == nil {\n137|\t\t\tt.Fatal(\"DecodeSpawnPlan admitted 513-character mapping\")\n138|\t\t}\n139|\t\tif !strings.Contains(err.Error(), \"not at most 512 characters\") {\n140|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"DecodeSpawnPlan error = %v, want the mapping bound arm\", err)\n141|\t\t}\n142|\t})\n143|\tt.Run(\"provhost mapping admits 300 wide characters\", func(t *testing.T) {\n144|\t\t// 300 `é` is 300 characters but 600 bytes: the bound\n145|\t\t// arm must admit it (runes) and the equality arm must\n146|\t\t// refuse it (it is not the provider mapping). A byte\n147|\t\t// measure would fire the bound arm instead.\n148|\t\twide := validSpawnJSON(strings.Repeat(\"é\", 300), \"\", \"\", \"\")\n149|\t\terr := provhost.DecodeSpawnPlan(wide, \"codex\", provhost.ProfileYOLO, scalar.PlatformLinux)\n150|\t\tif err == nil {\n151|\t\t\tt.Fatal(\"DecodeSpawnPlan admitted a mapping that is not the provider mapping\")\n152|\t\t}\n153|\t\tif !strings.Contains(err.Error(), \"does not match the provider profile\") {\n154|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"DecodeSpawnPlan error = %v, want the mapping equality arm, not the bound arm\", err)\n155|\t\t}\n156|\t})\n157|\tt.Run(\"provhost native session id bound\", func(t *testing.T) {\n158|\t\tmapping := validSpawnMapping(t)\n159|\t\taccept := validSpawnJSON(mapping, \"\", \"\", wide512)\n160|\t\tif err := provhost.DecodeSpawnPlan(accept, \"codex\", provhost.ProfileYOLO, scalar.PlatformLinux); err != nil {\n161|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"DecodeSpawnPlan refused 512-character native session id: %v\", err)\n162|\t\t}\n163|\t\trefuse := validSpawnJSON(mapping, \"\", \"\", wide513)\n164|\t\terr := provhost.DecodeSpawnPlan(refuse, \"codex\", provhost.ProfileYOLO, scalar.PlatformLinux)\n165|\t\tif err == nil {\n166|\t\t\tt.Fatal(\"DecodeSpawnPlan admitted 513-character native session id\")\n167|\t\t}\n168|\t\tif !strings.Contains(err.Error(), \"1..512 characters\") {\n169|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"DecodeSpawnPlan error = %v, want the native session id bound arm\", err)\n170|\t\t}\n171|\t})\n172|\tt.Run(\"identity opaque bound agrees\", func(t *testing.T) {\n173|\t\t// The opaque_identity value bound (1..1024 runes) is\n174|\t\t// the one member validated by both identity dialects:\n175|\t\t// both judges must agree on the multibyte edges.\n176|\t\taccept := mutateMember(t, validIdentityJSON(), \"opaque_identity\", `{\"k\":`+jsonQuote(wide1024)+`}`)\n177|\t\tif err := provhost.CheckIdentity(accept, \"antigravity\"); err != nil {\n178|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"CheckIdentity refused 1024-character opaque value: %v\", err)\n179|\t\t}\n180|\t\tif _, _, err := canonicaljson.CalculateObjectIdentity(accept); err != nil {\n181|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"CalculateObjectIdentity refused 1024-character opaque value: %v\", err)\n182|\t\t}\n183|\t\trefuse := mutateMember(t, validIdentityJSON(), \"opaque_identity\", `{\"k\":`+jsonQuote(wide1025)+`}`)\n184|\t\tif err := provhost.CheckIdentity(refuse, \"antigravity\"); err == nil {\n185|\t\t\tt.Fatal(\"CheckIdentity admitted 1025-character opaque value\")\n186|\t\t}\n187|\t\tif _, _, err := canonicaljson.CalculateObjectIdentity(refuse); err == nil {\n188|\t\t\tt.Fatal(\"CalculateObjectIdentity admitted 1025-character opaque value\")\n189|\t\t}\n190|\t})\n191|}\n192|\n193|// TestByteBoundsStayBytes proves the three ledgered byte gates\n194|// keep measuring bytes: each vector is within the rune bound a\n195|// character measure would enforce but over the byte bound the\n196|// specification states, so a rune-measure regression would admit\n197|// it and travel to a later arm instead of the byte arm.\n198|func TestByteBoundsStayBytes(t *testing.T) {\n199|\tmapping := validSpawnMapping(t)\n200|\tt.Run(\"argv element bytes\", func(t *testing.T) {\n201|\t\t// 2049 `é` is 2049 characters but 4098 bytes.\n202|\t\tbody := validSpawnJSON(mapping, strings.Repeat(\"é\", 2049), \"\", \"\")\n203|\t\terr := provhost.DecodeSpawnPlan(body, \"codex\", provhost.ProfileYOLO, scalar.PlatformLinux)\n204|\t\tif err == nil {\n205|\t\t\tt.Fatal(\"DecodeSpawnPlan admitted a 4098-byte argv element\")\n206|\t\t}\n207|\t\tif !strings.Contains(err.Error(), \"NUL-free bytes\") {\n208|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"DecodeSpawnPlan error = %v, want the argv element byte arm\", err)\n209|\t\t}\n210|\t})\n211|\tt.Run(\"argv total bytes\", func(t *testing.T) {\n212|\t\t// Seventeen 4000-byte elements pass the element gate\n213|\t\t// and fail the 65536-byte total.\n214|\t\telements := make([]string, 0, 17)\n215|\t\tfor index := 0; index < 17; index++ {\n216|\t\t\telements = append(elements, jsonQuote(strings.Repeat(\"a\", 4000)))\n217|\t\t}\n218|\t\tbody := []byte(fmt.Sprintf(`{\"argv\":[\"--serve\",%s],\"cwd\":\"/tmp/ax\",\"env_names\":[],\"env_literals\":{},\"native_session_id\":null,\"profile_mapping\":%s,\"extensions\":{}}`,\n219|\t\t\tstrings.Join(elements, \",\"), jsonQuote(mapping)))\n220|\t\terr := provhost.DecodeSpawnPlan(body, \"codex\", provhost.ProfileYOLO, scalar.PlatformLinux)\n221|\t\tif err == nil {\n222|\t\t\tt.Fatal(\"DecodeSpawnPlan admitted argv over 65536 total bytes\")\n223|\t\t}\n224|\t\tif !strings.Contains(err.Error(), \"65536 bytes total\") {\n225|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"DecodeSpawnPlan error = %v, want the argv total byte arm\", err)\n226|\t\t}\n227|\t})\n228|\tt.Run(\"env literal bytes\", func(t *testing.T) {\n229|\t\tbody := validSpawnJSON(mapping, \"\", strings.Repeat(\"é\", 2049), \"\")\n230|\t\terr := provhost.DecodeSpawnPlan(body, \"codex\", provhost.ProfileYOLO, scalar.PlatformLinux)\n231|\t\tif err == nil {\n232|\t\t\tt.Fatal(\"DecodeSpawnPlan admitted a 4098-byte env literal\")\n233|\t\t}\n234|\t\tif !strings.Contains(err.Error(), \"4096 NUL-free bytes\") {\n235|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"DecodeSpawnPlan error = %v, want the env literal byte arm\", err)\n236|\t\t}\n237|\t})\n238|}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
