{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c6f5","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07664-b32a-7b03-be28-978067559ac9"},"sequence":469,"recorded_at":1780531400000933,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"4279c805-073c-4405-a747-7b1a47e438ac","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"4279c805-073c-4405-a747-7b1a47e438ac","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"4279c805-073c-4405-a747-7b1a47e438ac"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"1c737663-f0f7-48c7-825a-5471fe135ad8"},"task_id":"1c737663-f0f7-48c7-825a-5471fe135ad8","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"1c737663-f0f7-48c7-825a-5471fe135ad8","chunk":"Read text file `/tmp/mutlog.md`.\n1|# Mutation battery log — TASK-260830-3bkz0c\n2|\n3|Harness: `.temp/TASK-260830-3bkz0c/mut.sh` (scoped to\n4|`internal/environ`; restores from `/tmp/env-baseline` after every\n5|run). Each mutant applied by its named python script with a\n6|count==1 exact-match assertion (NOT-APPLIED if no textual\n7|change). Gate: `go test ./internal/environ/ -count=1`.\n8|Baseline tree sha: `.temp/TASK-260830-3bkz0c/pre-battery.sha`;\n9|post-battery sha identical (`diff` empty → TREE_IDENTICAL).\n10|\n11|## Narrowing mutants (gate stays present, admits exactly one member of the rejected class)\n12|\n13|| Mutant | Narrowing | Named failing test | Result |\n14||---|---|---|---|\n15|| N1 `n1_lowsurrogate.py`: drop the low-surrogate arm of the gate (admits lone lows, keeps refusing highs) | lone-low escapes | TestFrameAgreementAcrossFacades/bare_low_escape | KILLED |\n16|| N2 `n2_bytelength.py`: StringLength counts bytes, not runes | 128-char/256-byte values | TestStringMeasureCountsRunes/environ_helper | KILLED |\n17|| N3 `n3_tuplextensions.py`: tuple admits `extensions` member | one unknown member | TestTupleAgreementAcrossFacades/extensions_refused | KILLED |\n18|| N4 `n4_caplength.py`: capabilities length check `<` instead of `!=` (admits 9-key map) | ninth capability | TestDecodeEnvironmentObservation/ninth_capability_refused | KILLED |\n19|| N6 `n6_envunderscore.py`: env-id grammar admits `_` | underscore ids | TestSharedGrammarsAreOneLanguage | KILLED |\n20|| T1 `t1_rawscan.py`: gate keeps its name and refusal texts but matches `\\u` byte pairs without consuming `\\\\` pairs (raw-scan semantics) | escaped-backslash text | TestFrameAgreementAcrossFacades/escaped_backslash_{high,low,pair}_run2, _in_member_name, _nested (5 rows); TestSharedImplementationsAreCensused still PASSES under T1 | KILLED |\n21|\n22|T1 is the token-preserving attack on the census source-text\n23|gate: the symbol `HasLoneSurrogateEscape` stays defined, so a\n24|grep-level gate would pass, while the behavioral suite fails on\n25|exactly the escaped-backslash class. Census + behavior are\n26|complementary by construction, not by assertion.\n27|\n28|## Existence-only (not accepted as narrowing evidence)\n29|\n30|| Mutant | What it proves | Result |\n31||---|---|---|\n32|| D1 `d1_deletegate.py`: remove the surrogate-gate call (gate absent) | gate exists | KILLED (bare_high/low, high-followed-by-non-low, run3 rows) — existence only, excluded from the narrowing claim |\n33|\n34|## Totals\n35|\n36|Applied 7, killed 7. Narrowing kills 6 of 6 (N1, N2, N3, N4,\n37|N6, T1). Census-only kills 0 (no census-only mutant run).\n38|Over-applied (mutant fails to apply): 0. Survivors: none.\n39|Every surviving-mutant bound is therefore vacuous; no bound\n40|needs stating."}}}
