arm `internal/environ/decode.go:104-108` names as the gate's reason to\n85|exist. Found by differential fuzz (400k vectors, seed 20260906) against\n86|`HasLoneSurrogateEscape`, then reduced to the deterministic witness above.\n87|\n88|Why the battery is green over it: `frameCorpus()` samples backslash-run parity\n89|(run 1 / 2 / 3) but never composes an **even run with a following real escape**.\n90|`escaped backslash high run2` is `A\\\\ud800B` — literal text, nothing after it. The\n91|class was sampled on the over-strict side only and the safe conclusion was\n92|inferred from that sample. That is the \"property inferred from an incomplete\n93|sample, reported as established\" shape, and it is the specific defect this leaf\n94|was created to catch — leaf 1's one-directional\n95|`TestSurrogateGateAgreesWithCanonicalJSON` is named in the brief for hiding\n96|exactly this class, and the replacement battery hides the more dangerous half of it.\n97|\n98|To close: add the composed shape to `frameCorpus()` with the real per-judge\n99|verdicts, correct the ledger text in `census_test.go`, `doc.go`, `boundary.md`\n100|and the LOGBOOK entry to say the divergence is **bidirectional and includes an\n101|admission hole**, and — B2b — record the frozen-scanner unification as a **board\n102|element**. It currently exists only as prose (\"Genuinely-required frozen-package\n103|change (not made)\") in `boundary.md` and the LOGBOOK; there is no board item for\n104|it. The freeze is a legitimate reason not to fix the scanners in this leaf; it is\n105|not a reason to ledger the class as harmless.\n106|\n107|## F1 (must fix, non-blocking on its own) — the library is behind nothing, and says otherwise\n108|\n109|No file outside `internal/environ` imports it. The only occurrence of the import\n110|path anywhere else in the tree is inside an error string in `census_test.go:241`.\n111|Six production functions sit at **0.0%** statement coverage — no production\n112|caller and no test:\n113|